Subject: [PATCH] libostree: add an explicit systemd-boot backend

Register systemd-boot as an explicitly selected OstreeBootloader. Delegate
preparation and publication to the separately installed
${prefix}/lib/ostree/ostree-systemd-boot helper, using the existing write_config
and post_bls_sync hooks respectively. Preserve helper exit errors with command
and output context, and report the backend as non-atomic.

Force a new bootversion for non-noop writes so userspace-only deployment
changes cannot bypass the helper through the bootlink-only optimization.
Preparation sees the new BLS entries and populated bootlinks; publication runs
only after the root BLS switch is synchronized. Recover interrupted publication
before deployment writes or cleanup can remove referenced deployments or boot
configurations. The helper recovers only a prepared generation with a pending
marker in the active root BLS generation. Initial installation remains an
installer operation via the helper's install command.

Teach the fstab generator to recognize exact stable systemd-boot selectors,
read their symlinks below the physical /sysroot, and validate deployment targets
before extracting the stateroot. Leave the standard BLS bootlink parser intact.

Include the matching Makefile.in registration to avoid autoreconf and new
host build dependencies for the release tarball.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream systemd-boot helper protocol]

