-          <literal>zipl</literal>.
+          <literal>zipl</literal>. The <literal>systemd-boot</literal> backend must be
+          explicitly selected and is never probed by <literal>auto</literal>.
+        </para>
+        <para>
+          The <literal>systemd-boot</literal> backend runs
+          <literal>/usr/lib/ostree/ostree-systemd-boot prepare SYSROOT BOOTVERSION</literal>
+          after writing BLS fragments to
+          <literal>SYSROOT/boot/loader.BOOTVERSION/entries</literal> and populating the
+          new bootlinks. The helper creates stable deployment symlinks independent of
+          the rotating bootlinks, copies and signs boot artifacts, and stages metadata.
+          After switching and synchronizing the root BLS configuration, OSTree runs
+          <literal>/usr/lib/ostree/ostree-systemd-boot commit SYSROOT BOOTVERSION</literal>
+          to publish the entries and default. The executable path uses the configured
+          installation prefix instead of <literal>/usr</literal> when different.
+          Every non-noop deployment write regenerates the bootloader configuration,
+          even when the kernel and arguments are unchanged. Updates are not atomic.
+          Before deployment writes or cleanup, the backend invokes
+          <literal>/usr/lib/ostree/ostree-systemd-boot recover SYSROOT</literal>
+          to complete any interrupted publication before referenced deployments or
+          boot configurations can be removed. Recovery checks
+          <literal>SYSROOT/boot/loader/systemd-boot/pending</literal> in the active
+          root BLS generation and does nothing if it is absent. Preparation persists
+          this marker last; commit removes it only after successful publication.
+          Recovery publishes the already prepared complete generation. A separate
+          boot service can invoke the same recovery command if the active marker
+          exists. These operations do not update EFI bootloader launchers.
+          The helper must be installed separately; the initial installer must run
+          <literal>/usr/lib/ostree/ostree-systemd-boot install-signed SYSROOT</literal> after
+          the initial deployment to configure <literal>sysroot.bootloader=systemd-boot</literal>
+          in the repository; use <literal>install-unsigned</literal> only for an explicitly unsigned installation.
         </para>
